{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KknYGDxyhntbTuVrh95EUg","type":"tool_result","content":"56-\n57-| Command | Purpose |\n58-|---|---|\n59:| `pose check [--strict\\|--tolerant]` | Structural integrity + matrix schema + task-map sync + spec graph + schema version |\n60-| `pose validate [--strict\\|--tolerant] [--stack s] [--module p\\|--workspace w\\|--root-only] [--changed-from A --changed-to B] [--explain] [--report [--report-task T]] [--json-out P] [--junit P] [--sarif P] [--emit-plan P]` | Run the validation matrix; `--report` writes a report that lists the commands this run executed and its result |\n61-| `pose lint-spec <slug>\\|--all [--ready-check] [--design-check]` | Section content and lifecycle gates; `--design-check` projects structured Assumption/Decision basis read-only with objective diagnostics |\n62-| `pose followups [--open\\|--all] [--overdue] [--owner @alias] [--fail-overdue] [--similarity N] [--json]` | Aggregate follow-ups, overdue triage dates and near-duplicate candidates |\n--\n237-validates structure and evidence, it never computes a score. Evidence uses\n238-typed references (`spec:`/`report:`/`adr:`/`knowledge:`/`doc:`/`commit:`/\n239-`check:`/`url:`); local types must resolve, the rest are syntactic\n240:(offline contract). `pose check --strict` runs the same validation when the\n241-artifact exists (opt-in by presence). Staleness thresholds live in\n242-`.pose/policy/capabilities.json` (defaults: 30 days / 200 commits).\n243-\n--\n284-the manifest's `default_review_days` counted from the doc's last touching\n285-commit. The security scan reuses the same deterministic, offline\n286-unsafe-instruction/secret-shaped pattern scan skills already run — defense\n287:in depth, not a substitute for the dedicated gitleaks gate. `pose check\n288---strict` incorporates `docs-check` when the manifest exists (opt-in by\n289-presence, same mechanic as capabilities); errors block, warnings surface\n290-without blocking. Tool MCP: `pose_docs_state`.\n--\n450-| **Result** | the verdict, the findings, the data a command was asked for | stdout |\n451-| **Progress** | steps, module headers, usage, and the command's own failures | stderr |\n452-\n453:For example, `pose check --json | jq` consumes the result channel. Keep stderr\n454-when diagnosing a failed invocation: progress and parser errors are not findings.\n455-\n456-| Flag / variable | Effect |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"70a75682-ba3b-4797-925e-ed7c02d00fac","timestamp":"2026-11-10T23:47:57.189Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"56-\n57-| Command | Purpose |\n58-|---|---|\n59:| `pose check [--strict\\|--tolerant]` | Structural integrity + matrix schema + task-map sync + spec graph + schema version |\n60-| `pose validate [--strict\\|--tolerant] [--stack s] [--module p\\|--workspace w\\|--root-only] [--changed-from A --changed-to B] [--explain] [--report [--report-task T]] [--json-out P] [--junit P] [--sarif P] [--emit-plan P]` | Run the validation matrix; `--report` writes a report that lists the commands this run executed and its result |\n61-| `pose lint-spec <slug>\\|--all [--ready-check] [--design-check]` | Section content and lifecycle gates; `--design-check` projects structured Assumption/Decision basis read-only with objective diagnostics |\n62-| `pose followups [--open\\|--all] [--overdue] [--owner @alias] [--fail-overdue] [--similarity N] [--json]` | Aggregate follow-ups, overdue triage dates and near-duplicate candidates |\n--\n237-validates structure and evidence, it never computes a score. Evidence uses\n238-typed references (`spec:`/`report:`/`adr:`/`knowledge:`/`doc:`/`commit:`/\n239-`check:`/`url:`); local types must resolve, the rest are syntactic\n240:(offline contract). `pose check --strict` runs the same validation when the\n241-artifact exists (opt-in by presence). Staleness thresholds live in\n242-`.pose/policy/capabil