DN87cQQbS2zTqPaMTHYwL","tool_input":{"command":"pose assess design --spec pose-commit-gate-refuses-index-without-descriptor --json 2>&1 | head -60","description":"Run the design assessment"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":23,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**decision: changes-requested**\n\nThe code change is small and reads correctly. I'm requesting changes for two medium-severity reasons: the required `artifact-check --strict` fails because one artifact in the spec is declared with the wrong action, and the spec says R1 is satisfied although its second message is never tested.\n\n## How I reviewed\n\n- I read the diff for `cs-1558a46c96a4`, the spec, `nativeChecker.failOrWarn`/`message` and `Store.ReadIndexGeneration` (`pose-mcp/internal/pose/index_generation.go:309-398`).\n- I ran `pose artifact-check --spec … --strict` and some `git log` / `merge-base` checks.\n- My permissions refused `go test`, `pose assess design` and plain `cat`/`grep` pipelines, so I did not run them. For test results I relied on the sealed evidence.\n- The range also contains commit `80b49143`, which changes the resident Git memo key. It belongs to another spec and isn't in this change set, so I didn't review it here.\n\n## Your questions\n\n- **False positive on a clean checkout:** none in the normal case. `.gitignore:27` ignores `.pose/indexes/generations/`, and `readGenerationFile` (`index_generation.go:335-351`) then falls back to the committed copies. If those match the descriptor, the status is `current` with nothing diverged, so there is no finding.\n  - Assumption I could not verify: the repo has no `.gitattributes`. A checkout that rewrites line endings (for example `core.autocrlf=true`) would change the bytes and make the set unavailable. That is true for every reader, not only the gate, so I count it as an accepted risk rather than a defect.\n- **Strict/tolerant split:** correct. The new check goes through `failOrWarn` (`check.go:71-77`): error in strict mode, warning in tolerant mode.\n- **Message:** correct, with one wording defect (F4).\n- **Manuals:** yes, they should mention it (F6).\n\n## Criteria\n\n| criterion | result | evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| assumption-integrity | passed | Clean-checkout fallback confirmed by reading (above). The line-ending risk is not verified and is accepted. |\n| backend-concurrency | finding (F5) | A read that runs while `pose index` is publishing can report a temporary divergence (`index_generation.go:152-156`). |\n| backend-contracts | passed | The check only adds findings to the existing renderer and `--json` path. Sealed `check-index-generation-integration`. |\n| backend-input-errors | passed | Every way the set can be unavailable reaches one bounded finding. |\n| backend-integration-impact | passed | Uses the same reader as all other index consumers. Sealed `index-generation-integrity-integration`. |\n| backend-observability | passed | The finding names the reason, the generation id, the affected files and the fix. |\n| compatibility | passed | The change is additive. Strict mode only gets stricter for a set that no reader can use anyway, and the changelog says so. |\n| correctness | passed | Both branches in `check.go:486-493` are correct by reading. Sealed build, unit and integration evidence. |\n| design-causality | passed | D1: reading the set's structure finds the harne8 failure without recomputing inputs (~20 s). |\n| documentation | finding (F6) | |\n| operability | finding (F4) | |\n| requirements | finding (F2) | |\n| scope | finding (F1) | |\n| security | passed | Read-only, paths come from fixed names, no secrets. |\n| solution-proportionality | passed | 17 lines that reuse the existing reader. |\n\n## Tools\n\n| tool | result | notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| artifact-check | failed | exit 1, `action-mismatch` (F1) |\n| validate (root) | passed | sealed `build:pose-mcp/go/build` |\n| validate [pose-mcp] | passed | sealed `unit:pose-mcp/go/test` |\n| review-check, closeout-check | deferred | They need the review to be finished. |\n| assess-design, assess-discover, assess-integrate, assess-tech-debt, suggest-review | not used | My permissions refused them. |\n\n## Defects\n\n- **F1 (medium, blocker)** – `.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-commit-gate-refuses-index-without-descriptor.md:50`: the spec lists the spec file as `created`. It was created in `af36fc0b`, which comes before the base `d40ca62a`, so it should be `modified`. Because of this, `pose artifact-check --strict` exits 1. The checker also resolved change set `cs-5faefbc8cd1a` with head `01f01cc5` instead of the bundle's `cs-1558a46c96a4` at `a6aca7ec`; worth checking when this is fixed.\n- **F2 (medium, blocker)** – `pose-mcp/internal/cli/check_index_generation_test.go:36-38` removes `generations/` before it edits the file. That means only the \"index set unavailable\" branch runs. The \"index files differ from generation\" branch (`check.go:490-491`) has no test, yet the spec says R1 is satisfied (spec line 92). One more case would cover it: run `pose index`, edit one file under `.pose/indexes/`, and assert the message, the file name and a non-zero exit code.\n- **F3 (low)** – `check_index_generation_test.go:50-53`: the tolerant run only checks that the text appears. It does not check that the finding is a warning (exit code or finding state), which is what R3 requires.\n- **F4 (low)** – `pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go:489`: some reasons already end with \"; run `pose index`\" (`index_generation.go:364`), so the message repeats the fix. Also, the reason text stays in English when the locale is pt-BR.\n- **F5 (low)** – `check.go:490`: if `pose index` is publishing at the same moment, a strict check can report \"differ from generation\" for a set that is fine a moment later. The \"run `pose index`\" advice is then misleading.\n- **F6 (low)** – `docs-site/docs/cli.md:59` and `POSE.md:215` describe `pose check` without the new index-set check.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"F1\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"disposition\": \"blocker\", \"file\": \".pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-commit-gate-refuses-index-without-descriptor.md\", \"line\": 50, \"summary\": \"The spec file is declared 'created' but was created in af36fc0b before base d40ca62a; pose artifact-check --strict exits 1 with action-mismatch. Declare it 'modified'.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F2\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"disposition\": \"blocker\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/check_index_generation_test.go\", \"line\": 36, \"summary\": \"The R1 'index files differ from generation <id>' branch (check.go:490-491) is never exercised: the test removes generations/ first, so only the unavailable branch runs, yet the requirement trace marks R1 satisfied.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F3\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/check_index_generation_test.go\", \"line\": 50, \"summary\": \"The R3 test asserts only that the tolerant output mentions the finding, not that it is a warning (exit code or finding state).\", \"action\": \"Assert the warning state or exit code of the tolerant run\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F4\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\", \"line\": 489, \"summary\": \"Some reasons already end with '; run `pose index`' (index_generation.go:364), so the message repeats the fix; the reason stays English under the pt-BR locale.\", \"action\": \"Avoid the repeated fix hint and localize or mark the reason\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F5\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\", \"line\": 490, \"summary\": \"A strict check that runs while pose index is publishing can report a temporary divergence (index_generation.go:152-156) with misleading 'run pose index' advice.\", \"action\": \"Distinguish an in-flight publication (lock held) from a diverged set, or document it\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F6\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"docs-site/docs/cli.md\", \"line\": 59, \"summary\": \"The pose check descriptions in cli.md:59 and POSE.md:215 omit the new index-set check.\", \"action\": \"Mention the index-set check in cli.md and POSE.md (and locales)\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"}\n  ],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"assumption-integrity\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-index-generation-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Verified: on a clean checkout readGenerationFile falls back to the committed copies when generations/ is gitignored (.gitignore:27), so a matching set gives no finding. Unverified, accepted risk: there is no .gitattributes, so line-ending rewriting would make the set unavailable for every reader, not only the gate.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-concurrency\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F5\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-contracts\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-index-generation-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-input-errors\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-index-generation-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/index-generation-integrity-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-observability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-index-generation-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"compatibility\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-index-generation-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined check.go:147 and 479-493: the change only adds findings through the existing renderer and JSON path. Strict mode gets stricter only for a set no reader can use; the changelog records the change.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"correctness\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-index-generation-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"design-causality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-75651ca0a8b75886\", \"rationale\": \"Under D1 (basis R1, R2) the gate reads only the set's structure through ReadIndexGeneration, which finds the harne8 state (descriptor not describing its files) without recomputing inputs. A stale set is not reported, as the spec intends.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"documentation\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F6\"},\n    {\"id\": \"operability\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F4\"},\n    {\"id\": \"requirements\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"scope\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"security\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-index-generation-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the new check: it is read-only, paths come from fixed index names under the root, the output holds only file names, generation ids and digests, and there are no secrets or authority changes.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"solution-proportionality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-index-generation-integration\", \"rationale\": \"17 lines reuse the existing reader. The smaller alternative (index --verify) costs about 20 s and flags normal staleness. The choice is invalidated if a commit leaves the set unreadable and still passes strict check, which the integration test guards for the unavailable branch.\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"artifact-check\", \"disposition\": \"failed\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-commit-gate-refuses-index-without-descriptor --strict\", \"rationale\": \"Exit 1: action-mismatch on the spec file declared created (F1).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-design\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"The reviewer's permissions refused the command; the sealed structure evidence was used instead.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"The reviewer's permissions refused the command.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-integrate\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"The reviewer's permissions refused the command; sealed integration evidence was used instead.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"The reviewer's permissions refused the command.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"closeout-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Requires the review to be complete.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"review-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Requires the review to be complete.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"The reviewer's permissions refused the command.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"build:pose-mcp/go/build\", \"rationale\": \"Sealed strict validation run.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"Sealed strict validation run of pose-mcp.\"}\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":1480,"type":"result","duration_ms":243892,"uuid":"a27dd778-d2e2-483c-a76d-916167eb85e0","ttft_stream_ms":957,"time_to_request_ms":47,"first_content_frame_ms":957,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":32,"outputTokens":13878,"cacheReadInputTokens":658126,"cacheCreationInputTokens":53228,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.8351371999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":5713,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":53228,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-04T10:05:09.044Z"}
